1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,905
Hi Jun.

2
00:00:00,905 --> 00:00:05,884
As you know, I've asked you here today to discuss the future of our

3
00:00:05,884 --> 00:00:06,620
Self-Access Centre.

4
00:00:06,620 --> 00:00:11,881
We have to decide what we want to do about this very important resource

5
00:00:11,881 --> 00:00:13,760
for our English language students.

6
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:17,710
So, can you tell me what the students think about this?

7
00:00:17,710 --> 00:00:21,440
Well, from the students' point of view, we would like to keep it.

8
00:00:21,440 --> 00:00:24,985
The majority of students say that they enjoy using it

9
00:00:24,985 --> 00:00:29,948
because it provides a variation on the classroom routine and they see it as

10
00:00:29,948 --> 00:00:32,430
a pretty major component of their course,

11
00:00:32,430 --> 00:00:37,108
but we would like to see some improvements to the equipment, particularly the computers;

12
00:00:37,108 --> 00:00:41,786
there aren't enough for one each at the moment and we always have to

13
00:00:41,786 --> 00:00:42,120
share.

14
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:45,978
Well yes, the teachers agree that it is a very valuable resource

15
00:00:45,978 --> 00:00:50,479
but one thing we have noticed is that a lot of the students are

16
00:00:50,479 --> 00:00:52,730
using it to check their personal emails.

17
00:00:52,730 --> 00:00:55,722
We don't want to stop you students using it,

18
00:00:55,722 --> 00:01:00,378
but we think the computers should be used as a learning resource, not for

19
00:01:00,378 --> 00:01:00,710
emails.

20
00:01:00,710 --> 00:01:06,024
Some of us also think that we could benefit a lot more by relocating

21
00:01:06,024 --> 00:01:09,440
the Self-Access Centre to the main University library building.

22
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:12,000
How do you think the students would feel about that, Jun?

23
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,257
Well, the library is big enough to incorporate the Self-Access Centre,

24
00:01:16,257 --> 00:01:19,740
but it wouldn't be like a class activity anymore.

25
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:24,733
Our main worry would be not being able to go to a teacher for

26
00:01:24,733 --> 00:01:25,090
advice.

27
00:01:25,090 --> 00:01:28,190
I'm sure there would be plenty of things to do

28
00:01:28,190 --> 00:01:31,910
but we really need teachers to help us choose the best activities.

29
00:01:31,910 --> 00:01:34,527
Well, there would still be a teacher present and he

30
00:01:34,527 --> 00:01:38,191
or she would guide the activities of the students, we wouldn't just leave them

31
00:01:38,191 --> 00:01:39,500
to get on with it.

32
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:39,550
Yes,

33
00:01:39,550 --> 00:01:43,670
but I think the students would be much happier keeping the existing set-up;

34
00:01:43,670 --> 00:01:47,812
they really like going to the Self-Access Centre with their teacher

35
00:01:47,812 --> 00:01:51,200
and staying together as a group to do activities.

36
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:55,692
If we could just improve the resources and facilities, I think it would be

37
00:01:55,692 --> 00:01:56,013
fine.

38
00:01:56,013 --> 00:01:58,580
Is the cost going to be a problem?

39
00:01:58,580 --> 00:02:01,795
It's not so much the expense that I'm worried about,

40
00:02:01,795 --> 00:02:04,367
and we've certainly got room to do it,

41
00:02:04,367 --> 00:02:08,868
but it's the problem of timetabling a teacher to be in there outside class

42
00:02:08,868 --> 00:02:09,190
hours.

43
00:02:09,190 --> 00:02:12,503
If we're going to spend a lot of money on equipment

44
00:02:12,503 --> 00:02:16,720
and resources, we really need to make sure that everything is look after properly.

45
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:21,573
Anyway, let's make some notes to see just what needs doing to improve the

46
00:02:21,573 --> 00:02:21,920
Centre.

47
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:23,867
Now, what about the computers?

48
00:02:23,867 --> 00:02:28,930
I think it might be a good idea to install some new models.

49
00:02:28,930 --> 00:02:34,233
They would take up a lot less room and so that would increase the work space for text books

50
00:02:34,233 --> 00:02:35,070
and so on.

51
00:02:35,070 --> 00:02:36,104
That would be great.

52
00:02:36,104 --> 00:02:38,430
It is a bit cramped in there at times.

53
00:02:38,430 --> 00:02:39,681
What about other resources?

54
00:02:39,681 --> 00:02:44,057
Do you have a list of things that the students would like to see

55
00:02:44,057 --> 00:02:44,370
improved?

56
00:02:44,370 --> 00:02:49,695
Yes, one of the comments that students frequently make is that they find if

57
00:02:49,695 --> 00:02:54,640
difficult to find materials that are appropriate for their level, especially reading resources.

58
00:02:54,640 --> 00:02:57,330
So I think we need to label them more clearly.

59
00:02:57,330 --> 00:02:57,644
Well,

60
00:02:57,644 --> 00:03:00,780
that's easy enough, we can get that organised very quickly.

61
00:03:00,780 --> 00:03:05,233
In fact I think we should review all of the study resources as some

62
00:03:05,233 --> 00:03:07,460
of them are looking a bit out-of-date.

63
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:07,879
Definitely.

64
00:03:07,879 --> 00:03:11,650
The CD section especially needs to be more current.

65
00:03:11,650 --> 00:03:17,166
I think we should get some of the ones that go with our latest course books

66
00:03:17,166 --> 00:03:18,890
and also make multiple copies.

67
00:03:18,890 --> 00:03:23,611
Good, now I was also thinking about some different materials that we haven't got

68
00:03:23,611 --> 00:03:24,960
in there at all.

69
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:29,560
What do you think of the idea of introducing some workbooks?

70
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:34,582
If we break them up into separate pages and laminate them, they'd be a

71
00:03:34,582 --> 00:03:35,300
great resource.

72
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:38,958
The students could study the main course book in class

73
00:03:38,958 --> 00:03:42,250
and then do follow-up practice in the Self-Access Centre.

74
00:03:42,250 --> 00:03:43,379
That sounds good.

75
00:03:43,379 --> 00:03:48,270
——Okay, now finally we need to think about how the room is used.

76
00:03:48,270 --> 00:03:52,784
I'll have to talk to the teachers and make sure we can all reach

77
00:03:52,784 --> 00:03:56,330
some agreement on a timetable to supervise the centre after class.

78
00:03:56,330 --> 00:03:59,243
But we also need to think about security, too.

79
00:03:59,243 --> 00:04:02,480
Especially if we're going to invest in some new equipment.

80
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:05,160
What about putting in an alarm?

81
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:05,887
Good idea.

82
00:04:05,887 --> 00:04:10,250
The other thing I'd like to do is talk to our technicians

83
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:14,250
and see whether we could somehow limit the access to email.

84
00:04:14,250 --> 00:04:17,330
I really don't want to see that resource misused.

85
00:04:17,330 --> 00:04:21,650
What about if we agree to only use it before and after class?

86
00:04:21,650 --> 00:04:22,066
Yes,

87
00:04:22,066 --> 00:04:23,732
that would be fine.

88
00:04:23,732 --> 00:04:26,230
OK, anyway… that's great for now.

89
00:04:26,230 --> 00:04:28,950
We'll discuss it further when we've managed to…
